1
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,600
Strict JSON, from the punctuation up. Six value kinds, and why valid is only the first check

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:13,100
The chapter's example ticket. One object, with named members inside.

3
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,200
Number, boolean, null, string, array, object. That is all JSON has.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,666
null has no quotes. "null" in quotes would be a four-letter string.

5
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:22,166
Braces enclose an object, brackets an array. Indentation is only for readers.

6
00:00:22,666 --> 00:00:24,666
Objects are unordered name/value pairs. If order matters, use an array.

7
00:00:27,166 --> 00:00:31,166
It looks like a Python dictionary. A JSON parser rejects it.

8
00:00:31,666 --> 00:00:34,466
Two separate errors. A parser reports the first place it gets stuck.

9
00:00:34,966 --> 00:00:37,166
Double quotes, no final comma: valid JSON.

10
00:00:37,666 --> 00:00:40,066
Some parsers accept extensions, so "my parser accepted it" doesn't prove it is portable.

11
00:00:45,966 --> 00:00:47,466
Four objects about ticket 1004 that say four different things.

12
00:00:47,966 --> 00:00:50,166
Is missing the same as null? JSON doesn't decide. The application's contract does.

13
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:52,866
An empty events list doesn't say whether history is absent or just not included.

14
00:00:55,366 --> 00:00:59,166
JSON has no date type. A timestamp is text in an agreed format.

15
00:00:59,666 --> 00:01:01,866
MongoDB stores BSON, which has Date and ObjectId types. The sender decides.

16
00:01:02,366 --> 00:01:05,166
Don't assume a date-looking string quietly becomes a Date.

17
00:01:05,666 --> 00:01:08,066
Valid JSON, a good document model, and a stored BSON document are three different claims.

18
00:01:09,666 --> 00:01:19,666
Remember: Six kinds: object, array, string, number, true/false, null. Double quotes only. No trailing commas, comments, NaN, or dates. Missing, null, [ ] and 0 can mean different things: define the contract. JSON has no date type. MongoDB stores BSON, which does. Valid syntax is not a good data model.

